<title>USA: Hughes, Raytheon venture gets $80 mln deal.</title>
<headline>Hughes, Raytheon venture gets $80 mln deal.</headline>
<dateline>HUNTSVILLE, Ala. 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>MEADS Inc said on Thursday that it has been awarded $80 million to conduct the MEADS Project Definition-Validation Program under contract to the NATO Medium Extended Air Defense System Management Agency.</p>
<p>The MEADS team includes H&amp;R Co, which is a joint venture between Hughes Aircraft Co and Raytheon Co, DASA-LFK, Siemens AG and Alenia of Italy.</p>
<p>The PD-V program is planned to culminate in a January 1999 International Source Selection to downselect to a single contractor team for Design and Development and System Production with an estimated value greater than $6 billion.</p>
<p>Hughes Aircraft is a unit of Hughes Electronics Corp.</p>
